    "answer": {
      "short": "$c=x$, where $x\\ne0,1$.\n\nUse $b-1=\\dfrac{a}{1-a}$, then simplify $c=\\dfrac{b}{b-1}=\\dfrac1a$.",
      "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}b-1&=\\dfrac1{1-a}-1\\\\b-1&=\\dfrac{1-(1-a)}{1-a}\\\\b-1&=\\dfrac{a}{1-a}.\\end{align*}$$\n$$\\begin{align*}c&=\\dfrac{b}{b-1}\\\\c&=\\dfrac{\\dfrac1{1-a}}{\\dfrac{a}{1-a}}\\\\c&=\\dfrac1{1-a}\\times\\dfrac{1-a}{a}\\\\c&=\\dfrac1a\\\\c&=\\dfrac1{\\frac{1}{x}}\\\\c&=x.\\end{align*}$$\nThe original definitions require $x\\ne0,1$.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
